Third-party assets
==================

The farm's sprites come from two asset packs by Kenney. Both are CC0, which asks
for no credit at all; this file gives it anyway, because the sprites are somebody
else's work and a reader of the farm should be able to find them.

The file in this repository derived from them is:

    app/src/main/resources/farm/atlas.png

It is the two packs' `Tilemap/tilemap_packed.png` stacked vertically, unchanged
pixel for pixel; `app/src/main/resources/farm/README.md` gives the recipe.

Tiny Town, version 1.1
    Author:  Kenney (www.kenney.nl)
    Pack:    https://kenney.nl/assets/tiny-town
    License: Creative Commons Zero, CC0 1.0 Universal
             http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
    Sheet:   rows 0-10 of the atlas, whole and unchanged
    Drawn:   three grass tiles for the ground, and the well's roof and base

Tiny Farm, version 1.0
    Author:  Kenney (www.kenney.nl)
    Pack:    https://kenney.nl/assets/tiny-farm
    License: Creative Commons Zero, CC0 1.0 Universal
             http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
    Sheet:   rows 11-21 of the atlas, whole and unchanged
    Drawn:   the tilled-soil furrows the fields are made of, four plants at
             four growth stages each, and the two farmers the villagers are
             drawn as

The atlas is the only asset in this repository that is anybody else's: there is
no bundled font, and the window draws its text with the system's.

Binary distributions
====================

The installers built from this repository (MSI, DMG, DEB) also carry a Java
runtime image and the project's own dependencies — Kotlin, Ktor, Netty, SQLite
JDBC, Compose Multiplatform and Skiko among them. Each is under its own licence,
which travels inside the artifact it came from; none is listed here, because a
list kept by hand would go stale on the next dependency bump.
